# BL-1102: 286 -> 99 *, 180 -> 66 validator, 10 -> 9 inproc. The validator no longer fires R13's self-probe (its 23 traced
# removals over a probe world) or M1's, so c-write is a one-receipt traced run like the others, the m1 and
# c-restricted-seeds starts are gone, and the probe-world build is gone from the in-process passes. Measured by one counted
# run through core/scripts/hermetic-run.sh (the judge's own J3 output) at this change's tip; the push's counted run is the
# second.
# BL-899 enumeration removal: 99 -> 111 *, 66 -> 73 validator. The new cell c-enum-unguarded is one start, one --score-one
# and three --r13-one workers (two named removals and the enumeration removal); pop-1 gains one --r13-one (world e's
# enumeration removal); c-committed's world follows DEFAULT_MAX_R13 (5 -> 6), so it gains one --r13-one and that removal's
# seeded receipt run. The rest of * is the seeded receipts those removals run. Measured the same way.
# Every distinct state is ONE FXCELL-tagged cli start of a validator copy (21 cells, cells.decl), its workers covered by
# the one self-nested row. c-m1-e2e and cli-wire drive real --score-one and --r13-one workers.
# inproc 12: untraced_fn 3 (one per r13_untraced call), m1_chain_fn 3 (one per m1_driver_absent call) and base_setup
# 3 per pass (vbr_sec_env, vbr_sec_args, vbr_sec_setup) x 2 passes = 6; every in-process call is paired with its own
# fx_inproc (arm P2).
# W6-11 (BL-899): 105 -> 106 *, 70 -> 71 validator, 9 -> 12 inproc, on W6-10's tree (DEFAULT_MAX_R13 = 3). World m's
# fourth receipt (`bash -e w/never2.sh`, EXCLUDED, no removal) is the one start-moving change, so it accounts for the
# +1 start and +1 validator start; the in-process cell c-m1-chain adds three fx_inproc passes and no start. Measured by one counted run through core/scripts/hermetic-run.sh
# at AI_DLC_FIXTURE_JOBS=12 (the judge's own J3 output).
# W12-14 (BL-899 variable-built reads): 106 -> 116 *, 71 -> 77 validator, inproc unchanged. The new cell c-var-built
# (22 cli cells now) is one start, one --score-one and four --r13-one workers (drv.sh, data.txt and the two
# variable-built reads, each removed alone), plus the seeded receipt runs those removals make. Measured by one counted
# run (scripts/seed-verdict-store.sh, the judge's own J3 output) at AI_DLC_FIXTURE_JOBS=12.
# 264-C: DEFAULT_MAX_R13 3 -> 0 (c-committed follows it): 116 -> 110 *, 77 -> 74 validator.
